  "published": "2026-11-11T20:17:18.86Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Added: field error codes, so a client can show validation errors in its own language. A validation 400 now carries errorCodes next to errors: the same keys, and for each message a { code, args } entry at the same index; errors keeps its exact shape, and errorCodes is left out when no field error has a code or args. New FieldError type (message, optional code, typed args through With) and Error.BadRequest(IReadOnlyDictionary<string, FieldError[]>) for field errors built in a handler; Error.FieldErrors reads them back. ResultCrafter.FluentValidation and WithValidation<T>() fill the code from each failure's ErrorCode (FluentValidation's validator name, such as NotEmptyValidator, when the rule sets none) and the rule's limits as args (minLength, maxLength when the rule has a maximum, from, to, expectedPrecision, expectedScale, and a comparisonValue that is neither a string nor another property); the attempted value is never copied. ProblemResponse documents errorCodes in OpenAPI (new FieldErrorCode schema type). Changed: two validation errors with the same messages but different codes or args are no longer equal. Error.BadRequest(IReadOnlyDictionary<string, string[]>) now throws ArgumentException for a null message instead of sending JSON null, which the errors schema does not allow. Update all ResultCrafter packages together: an older package next to a 3.1 one drops errorCodes and sends the 3.0 body. Guide: https://github.com/HaikAsatryan/ResultCrafter/blob/main/docs/guide.md#field-error-codes",
